From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AmberELEC <devnull@amberelec.org>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: Happy Eyeballs hostname resolution for stream connect

Streaming to a hostname that resolves to multiple addresses (several IPv6
plus IPv4, as published by Fritzbox DNS/mDNS) stalled: resolveHostName()
probed each resolved address serially with a 3s (TEST_PORT_TIMEOUT_SEC)
blocking connect. Unreachable IPv6 addresses therefore blocked ~3s each
before IPv4 was tried, causing "Connection timed out after 3 seconds" and
a subsequent RTSP reset (104), while an IPv4 literal connected instantly.

Replace the serial probe loop with a simplified Happy Eyeballs (RFC 8305)
racer: all candidates are probed with staggered non-blocking connects and
the first to complete wins. IPv4 is ordered slightly ahead of IPv6, and
unusable fe80::/10 link-local addresses (no scope id) are skipped. Pure
IPv4 and pure IPv6 hosts keep their previous single-address behaviour.
